WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.540
- Give me some okra and
some fried red snapper.

00:00:03.540 --> 00:00:04.950
And girl, you know I want some chitlins.

00:00:04.950 --> 00:00:06.990
- [Waitress] All right now.

00:00:06.990 --> 00:00:08.193
- Y'all got ham hocks?

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:10.380
- [Waitress] Of course.

00:00:10.380 --> 00:00:11.213
- Well, that's what I want.

00:00:11.213 --> 00:00:13.620
I want a plate of ham hocks,
deep-fried, blackened,

00:00:13.620 --> 00:00:15.450
and served on a bed of mustard greens.

00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:16.890
- Pig feet.

00:00:16.890 --> 00:00:20.400
I want some pig feet and
four pounds of grits.

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:21.413
And oh, oh! And-and you know what else?

00:00:21.413 --> 00:00:24.054
Give me a little Dixie cup full of lard.

00:00:24.054 --> 00:00:27.026
(upbeat beatbox music)

00:00:27.026 --> 00:00:29.790
(tense music)

00:00:29.790 --> 00:00:31.023
- Drew, come forward.

00:00:33.390 --> 00:00:34.223
- Yes, Chef.

00:00:34.223 --> 00:00:36.300
This is a chicken quiche
with cremini mushrooms,

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:38.263
baby spinach, and feta cheese.

00:00:38.263 --> 00:00:40.763
(tense music)

00:00:50.130 --> 00:00:50.963
- Unbelievable.

00:00:53.430 --> 00:00:56.174
Well, Drew, I have a huge
problem with this dish.

00:00:56.174 --> 00:00:58.140
(dramatic thud)
(suspenseful music)

00:00:58.140 --> 00:01:00.116
It's that you haven't
made it for me sooner.

00:01:00.116 --> 00:01:01.260
(uplifting music)

00:01:01.260 --> 00:01:02.160
- Thank you, Chef.

00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:04.740
- Because if you had, Drew,

00:01:04.740 --> 00:01:06.120
then I would know how good you are

00:01:06.120 --> 00:01:08.335
at cooking food that's bad.

00:01:08.335 --> 00:01:09.990
(dramatic thud)
(suspenseful music)

00:01:09.990 --> 00:01:10.980
- I'm sorry, Chef.

00:01:10.980 --> 00:01:13.608
- And when I say, "bad," I
mean, Michael Jackson bad.

00:01:13.608 --> 00:01:15.390
(uplifting music)

00:01:15.390 --> 00:01:16.380
- Thank you, Chef.

00:01:16.380 --> 00:01:18.090
- You know how he looked
really, really bad

00:01:18.090 --> 00:01:18.975
at the end of his life?

00:01:18.975 --> 00:01:21.030
(dramatic thud)
(suspenseful music)

00:01:21.030 --> 00:01:22.500
- Chef, I'm sorry.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:25.080
I don't know if you like the dish or not.

00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:27.390
- You don't know if I
like the dish or not?

00:01:27.390 --> 00:01:28.620
Well, let's put it this way.

00:01:28.620 --> 00:01:32.073
Pack your (bleep) knives,
get out, you're off the show.

00:01:32.073 --> 00:01:33.183
- Sorry, Chef.

00:01:35.160 --> 00:01:38.310
- Because you should be working

00:01:38.310 --> 00:01:40.512
in the finest restaurant in the world.

00:01:40.512 --> 00:01:41.790
(uplifting music)

00:01:41.790 --> 00:01:42.623
- Thank you, Chef.

00:01:42.623 --> 00:01:44.374
- Just not any world that I live in.

00:01:44.374 --> 00:01:45.600
(dramatic thud)
(suspenseful music)

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:46.433
- Sorry, Chef.

00:01:46.433 --> 00:01:49.410
- Because, frankly,
Drew, I'm jealous of you.

00:01:49.410 --> 00:01:50.880
- Thank you, Chef.

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:53.640
- And your ability to not give a (bleep)

00:01:53.640 --> 00:01:56.010
about what you cook.

00:01:56.010 --> 00:02:00.240
This is not fit for human consumption.

00:02:00.240 --> 00:02:04.170
No, this should be eaten
by a higher life-form

00:02:04.170 --> 00:02:06.120
with a more complex palate,

00:02:06.120 --> 00:02:07.980
but also an altruistic drive

00:02:07.980 --> 00:02:11.400
to save humanity from dishes like this.

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:14.995
Joking. Not! You deserve to die!

00:02:14.995 --> 00:02:17.730
(Gideon screaming)

00:02:17.730 --> 00:02:20.190
So you won't have to endure a life

00:02:20.190 --> 00:02:22.050
in which you will never exceed

00:02:22.050 --> 00:02:25.803
what you have achieved here today.

00:02:27.365 --> 00:02:30.198
(uplifting music)

00:02:35.250 --> 00:02:36.203
- Thank you, Chef.

00:02:39.420 --> 00:02:40.520
- In conclusion...

00:02:41.790 --> 00:02:43.393
Eh.

00:02:43.393 --> 00:02:45.060
- No, I'm good.

00:02:45.060 --> 00:02:45.893
- You hungry?

00:02:47.790 --> 00:02:49.050
- I could eat, yeah, man.

00:02:49.050 --> 00:02:51.450
Um, what you want? Uh...

00:02:51.450 --> 00:02:52.905
Pizza? Chinese?

00:02:52.905 --> 00:02:55.953
- (clicks tongue) Kill that noise, man.

00:02:59.010 --> 00:03:00.333
I got a Ratatouille.

00:03:02.186 --> 00:03:03.019
(rat squeaking)

00:03:03.019 --> 00:03:05.268
- Oh, (bleep)! That's a rat, dude!

00:03:05.268 --> 00:03:06.510
- Nah, it ain't.

00:03:06.510 --> 00:03:07.773
That's a Ratatouille, yo.

00:03:09.810 --> 00:03:12.780
Hey, Ratatouille, go
make my man a sandwich.

00:03:12.780 --> 00:03:15.577
Yeah, show him what you got.

00:03:15.577 --> 00:03:18.244
(rat squeaking)

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:23.400
- What the (bleep), son?

00:03:23.400 --> 00:03:25.203
You got a rat up in your house?

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:29.283
What does mean?

00:03:30.720 --> 00:03:32.970
- I don't know what to say, man.

00:03:32.970 --> 00:03:34.260
I got a Ratatouille, man.

00:03:34.260 --> 00:03:36.540
He a chef just like in
all that movies, man.

00:03:36.540 --> 00:03:39.600
- No, no. Hey, there's only...

00:03:39.600 --> 00:03:42.030
There's only one movie, Levi, all right?

00:03:42.030 --> 00:03:44.580
And he's not a ratatouille, he's a rat.

00:03:44.580 --> 00:03:46.620
And his name is Remy.

00:03:46.620 --> 00:03:47.760
- Potato, potato.

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:48.690
- Potato...

00:03:48.690 --> 00:03:51.753
- I gots myself some
Ratatouille, that's all I know.

00:03:52.792 --> 00:03:54.210
(rat squeaking)

00:03:54.210 --> 00:03:55.043
Order up.

00:03:55.043 --> 00:03:56.853
- [Cedric] Damn! Come on, Levi!

00:04:02.040 --> 00:04:02.873
- Voila.

00:04:04.890 --> 00:04:06.720
- Levi, look at this thing, man.

00:04:06.720 --> 00:04:09.420
You see it got bite marks all over it.

00:04:09.420 --> 00:04:11.910
- Any good chef has to taste his creation.

00:04:11.910 --> 00:04:16.620
- That's rat (bleep) on the sandwich.

00:04:16.620 --> 00:04:18.180
- He did make a sandwich, though.

00:04:18.180 --> 00:04:20.220
- Oh, hell no. I'm out.

00:04:20.220 --> 00:04:22.299
My dude, you need help.

00:04:22.299 --> 00:04:24.966
(playful music)

00:04:27.150 --> 00:04:30.333
