00:10:13.446 --> 00:10:14.656
- Claire!

00:10:14.656 --> 00:10:15.489
No!

00:10:23.340 --> 00:10:25.347
- Chinese it is.

00:10:25.347 --> 00:10:27.090
- I'm so glad we could bring this project

00:10:27.090 --> 00:10:28.110
to this neighborhood.

00:10:28.110 --> 00:10:29.970
- Oh, it's so rich in history.

00:10:29.970 --> 00:10:30.803
- Yeah.

00:10:30.803 --> 00:10:32.250
I grew up in a neighborhood like this.

00:10:32.250 --> 00:10:35.223
- Oh, yeah, I grew up in a
neighborhood exactly like this.

00:10:36.210 --> 00:10:38.100
- All right, welcome to Mama Sugarback's.

00:10:38.100 --> 00:10:38.970
Y'all ready to order?

00:10:38.970 --> 00:10:40.020
- Yeah.

00:10:40.020 --> 00:10:43.934
Can I have a chicken fried
steak with gravy and a cola?

00:10:43.934 --> 00:10:45.000
- Okay.

00:10:45.000 --> 00:10:48.000
- I will have the baked beef
short ribs with collard greens,

00:10:48.000 --> 00:10:50.250
and throw down some of that cornbread.

00:10:50.250 --> 00:10:52.320
- [Waitress] All right, babe.

00:10:52.320 --> 00:10:54.630
- You know what? Hold up a second.

00:10:54.630 --> 00:10:56.670
I'm also gonna have some
of them collard greens

00:10:56.670 --> 00:10:57.750
and cornbread as well,

00:10:57.750 --> 00:11:00.059
but hook a brother up with
some of them hot links.

00:11:00.059 --> 00:11:02.139
- All right.
- All right.

00:11:02.139 --> 00:11:05.340
- (chuckles) You know what?
Why am I trying to front?

00:11:05.340 --> 00:11:06.570
Scratch all that.

00:11:06.570 --> 00:11:10.050
Give me some okra and
some fried red snapper.

00:11:10.050 --> 00:11:11.460
And girl, you know I want some chitlins.

00:11:11.460 --> 00:11:13.500
- [Waitress] All right, now.

00:11:13.500 --> 00:11:14.673
- Y'all got ham hocks?

00:11:15.840 --> 00:11:16.860
- [Waitress] Of course.

00:11:16.860 --> 00:11:17.693
- Well, that's what I want.

00:11:17.693 --> 00:11:20.130
I want a plate of ham hocks,
deep-fried, blackened,

00:11:20.130 --> 00:11:21.960
and served on a bed of mustard greens.

00:11:21.960 --> 00:11:23.400
- Pig feet.

00:11:23.400 --> 00:11:26.880
I want some pig feet and
four pounds of grits.

00:11:26.880 --> 00:11:28.350
And oh, oh! And-and you know what else?

00:11:28.350 --> 00:11:31.230
Gimme a little Dixie cup
full of lard, all right?

00:11:31.230 --> 00:11:32.220
- I just remembered what I want.

00:11:32.220 --> 00:11:33.870
A bowl of mosquitoes.

00:11:33.870 --> 00:11:35.130
None of them tiny ones either,

00:11:35.130 --> 00:11:37.590
give me them big mother(bleep)
you find down at the swamps.

00:11:37.590 --> 00:11:40.890
- Sister, could you
please hook a brother up

00:11:40.890 --> 00:11:43.470
with a rusty bucket full of fish heads

00:11:43.470 --> 00:11:45.150
wrapped in razor wire?

00:11:45.150 --> 00:11:45.983
- Donkey teeth.

00:11:45.983 --> 00:11:46.890
- Donkey teeth?

00:11:46.890 --> 00:11:49.020
- Straight out a donkey's mouth.

00:11:49.020 --> 00:11:49.860
You know what? (bleep) it.

00:11:49.860 --> 00:11:51.420
Any animal tooth will do.

00:11:51.420 --> 00:11:53.070
I want you to stick it
in some honey glaze,

00:11:53.070 --> 00:11:54.090
fry it with fat back,

00:11:54.090 --> 00:11:55.770
and serve it in an old tin coffee can.

00:11:55.770 --> 00:11:58.080
- Forget everything I said
up to this point right now.

00:11:58.080 --> 00:12:01.230
Bring me some dandelion greens,
a cow hip, and a dog face.

00:12:01.230 --> 00:12:03.180
Wrap that whole mess in
an old Ebony magazine,

00:12:03.180 --> 00:12:04.620
and serve it to me in a shoebox.

00:12:04.620 --> 00:12:06.600
- Okay, I want a platter of stork ankles,

00:12:06.600 --> 00:12:09.420
an old cellar door, a possum spine,

00:12:09.420 --> 00:12:12.063
and a human foot.

00:12:17.760 --> 00:12:19.533
- You want a human foot?

00:12:21.000 --> 00:12:21.833
- Mm-hmm.

00:12:24.030 --> 00:12:25.893
- I got just one question for y'all.

00:12:31.020 --> 00:12:33.300
You want gravy on that cellar door?

00:12:33.300 --> 00:12:34.133
- Oh, definitely.

00:12:34.133 --> 00:12:35.417
- Oh, yeah, yeah, you
gotta put gravy on that.

00:12:35.417 --> 00:12:37.020
- What's a cellar door without gravy?

00:12:37.020 --> 00:12:38.090
- It's not food. (laughs)

00:12:38.090 --> 00:12:40.757
(dramatic thud)

00:12:47.430 --> 00:12:50.468
It's really... (chokes)

00:12:50.468 --> 00:12:53.718
(upbeat beatbox music)

00:12:55.988 --> 00:12:58.217
♪ All I want is ♪

00:12:58.217 --> 00:13:00.185
♪ But I don't need you ♪

